[#:seon.task{:name "delivered-errors-carry-no-result-handle",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "A core error recorded during an agent's call (another thread included) reaches the reply's `:seon.repl/errors` as `seon.error/value` plus count and branch, but with no result handle or dig form: the agent can reach the whole recorded error only by knowing to pull [`:seon.error/signature` s] with the observation selector. Reproduce: in SCI as agent X, @(future (`seon.fault/fault!` env (ex-info \"async\" {:probe/async 1}) {`:seon.agent/id` X ...})) answers :errors [{`:seon.error/signature` … `:seon.error/message` \"async\"}] without :probe/async or any handle. Correct (errors spec, 'Every error in a reply's :errors and :diagnostics carries its result handle'): each delivered error carries a handle or requery form that answers the whole recorded value. Proof: an evaluation that records a core fault answers :errors whose handle reads the fault's ex-data.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.render.transcript/branch-errors
              seon.turn/fault-window}}]
